{
  "requirement": "A provider failure that ends the model conversation returns\n`ValidationError::Agent` to the awaiting ask builder.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. When a provider failure ends the model conversation, the awaiting ask builder gets `ValidationError::Agent`.\n\n- **Main test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It builds a `ToolAgent` over `Script::new(vec![None])`. That script's `CompletionProvider::complete` returns `io::Error::other(\"permanent provider failure\")`. The test awaits `ctx.ask::<bool>()` and asserts the result matches `Err(ValidationError::Agent(error))`, with the provider's message in the error text. It also asserts that `ctx.dependencies()` is empty, so no typed result or dependency leaks from the failed ask. This checks both the error variant and that the failure is propagated.\n- **Setup-failure test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors]` is also marked. A missing credential makes the awaited `validation::verify` ask fail. It asserts `ValidationError::Agent(_)` and that the error text names the missing credential environment variable. It also shows that a deterministic refresh does not initialize the provider. This covers a second kind of provider failure, which comes through the configured-provider path.\n- **Unmarked tests:** I did not count tests that return `ValidationError::Agent` for submission-protocol violations. Those are not provider failures.\n- **Mid-conversation failure:** The provider failure in the main test happens on the first request, and no test makes it fail after earlier tool-call turns. The requirement does not distinguish where the failure occurs, so I do not treat this as a gap. The `Script` provider also supports multi-turn scripts, so such a test could be added.\n\nI found no unmet obligation and no marking gap.",
  "references": "0fbc2bd5fac34b56faf1a32f5f18e07e5f7165136fc32734f4466834b4898eda",
